{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed outbuilding, by reason of its excessive size and scale, inappropriate design and siting, and prominent position, would result in a visually intrusive and incongruous form of development that fails to respect the established character of the surrounding residential area. The proposal therefore would harm the character and appearance of the surrounding area, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 (Context and Character) and CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by virtue of the insufficient driveway depth, the lack of an adequate swept-path analysis demonstrating that vehicles could safely access and egress the site, and the absence of the required driver and pedestrian visibility splays, would result in unacceptable safety risks for pedestrians along a heavily used footway. The development therefore fails to provide safe, policy-compliant access and parking arrangements and is contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 and the Hounslow Residential Crossover and Off-Street Parking Policy."
  ],
